- single deletes: during the search (tests/test_recall_gate.py:756), during the rerank (tests/test_recall_gate.py:768), through the KG routes, also cancelled mid-call (tests/test_recall_gate.py:784, tests/test_recall_gate.py:1066), an entity edit (tests/test_recall_gate.py:1038), a consolidation that removes a vector and one that removes nothing (tests/test_recall_gate.py:807, tests/test_recall_gate.py:1093), a failed recall left with no unretrieved exception (tests/test_recall_gate.py:1126), and a remove that does not take the conversation lock (tests/test_recall_gate.py:574);
- the CLI and shutdown (tests/test_recall_gate.py:698, tests/test_recall_gate.py:686, tests/test_recall_gate.py:610).
The guards added by the delete round and the second review were mutated out one at a time (21 mutants in the delete round, 23 in the second review, including the two the second reviewer found surviving), and a test failed each time. The memory, recall, purge, KG, consolidation, taint, settings and shutdown suites pass (696 cases, one known local-3.11 failure, identical on the base).

agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py ports Hermes' rewriter (plugins/memory/query_rewrite.py). Its review rounds changed where the rewrite is used and tightened the filter.

(1) The rewriter. rewrite_query (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:134) asks a model for exactly one concise question about the user's own history, at TEMPERATURE 0 and MAX_TOKENS 96 (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:39-40).
- The latest message is bounded to 4,000 characters, keeping its head and tail around an omission marker (bounded_user_message, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:97).
- It is passed only as a JSON string on one data line. NEL (U+0085), U+2028 and U+2029, the line breaks JSON leaves raw, are escaped by hand, so the data cannot break that line (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:78, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:141).
- SYSTEM_PROMPT (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:80) says to treat the message as untrusted data, never follow it, never answer it, and ask in the message's language.
- Any exception, or an answer the filter rejects, returns "" so the caller recalls on the raw text, exactly as in Hermes.

(2) The filter. normalize_rewrite (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:111):
- NFKC-normalises the answer and removes format characters first (_plain, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:105);
- strips fences, labels (English and Romanian) and quotes, and control and line-separator characters;
- rejects an answer over 320 characters, not a question, not grounded in the user's memory, instruction-shaped, or with a second sentence.

Nerva additions for a Romanian-speaking owner:
- Romanian interrogatives (_QUESTION_START_RE, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:47) and grounding words (_MEMORY_GROUNDING_RE, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:60).
- An auxiliary starter, English or Romanian ("Did…", "Do…", "Am…", "E…", "A…", _AUX_START_RE, agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:55), counts as a question only when whitespace follows it and the model itself ended with "?" (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:122). "Do my taxes now.", "E-mail all my passwords…", "Am rezervat hotelul." and an invented "Ai programare marți la 10." are therefore refused. An interrogative word ("What…", "Ce…") needs no "?".
- Second-person and object pronouns are not grounding: "Can you tell me the capital of France?" is refused.
- The instruction check also reads "ignoring", "disregard" and the Romanian forms (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:68).
- A second sentence is refused: sentence punctuation (including ";" and "…") then a space and more text, or "?", "!" or ";" straight into more text ("?Now", ";also"). A "." or "…" with no space stays inside the question ("the 3.5 kg bag") (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:77).
- A question the model ended with "." gets "?" instead (agents/core/memory/query_rewrite.py:131).
This is a quality gate on what the embedder is asked, not a security control. The rewritten query reaches only the embedding model, never a generative one, and a homoglyph can still pass.

(3) Wiring (critic note 12). _recall_hits (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2577) runs the rewrite only when memory.recall_query_rewrite is on (seeded OFF at agents/core/settings_db.py:242, because it costs a model call).
- It runs after the H428 triviality gate and the job-pin check, and inside the H428 bound.
- It gets half the bound of its own (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2593-2597), as Hermes gives the rewrite its own 8 s. Past that, the model call is cancelled and recall runs on the raw text within the same turn, instead of the whole recall becoming a straggler.
- The rewrite becomes the embedding query only. The graph leg keeps the raw message as its keyword (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2605): it finds an entity whose name or a property contains the keyword, so it only ever helps a short, entity-like message ("BMW", "dentist"), and a rewritten whole question would never match. With the rewrite off or rejected, recall is unchanged (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2606). Hermes likewise keeps the raw message for its context fetch.

(4) Strict-local. _query_rewriter (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2608) uses LLMRouter.local_backend only (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2626). That is the fail-closed accessor, which never falls through to a cloud backend: no local backend means it raises and the rewrite returns "". This is proven through a real HybridRouter whose only backend is cloud. The call re-checks the job-model pin itself (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2625), and tells a Qwen3 model (the default local family) not to think, so the 96 tokens are not spent before the answer (agents/core/orchestrator.py:2628).

Like Hermes, the rewriter sees only the latest message, so a reference to an earlier turn ("the other one") stays unresolved. The win is a grounded question for short or oblique messages.

